<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
<p>PlugTheList (the "Platform") is operated by <?= e($v['company']) ?>, <?= e($v['address']) ?> ("we", "us"). The Platform is a marketplace. Curators (owners of playlists, channels and communities) offer promotional services. Creatives (artists, labels and businesses) buy them. We are not a party to the service itself, and curators are independent persons, not our employees or agents.</p>
<h2>2. Accounts</h2>
<p>You must be 18 or older, give accurate information and keep your password and two-step codes private. You are responsible for activity on your account. One person, one account. We may suspend accounts that break these terms or the Acceptable Use Policy.</p>
<h2>3. What curators may sell</h2>
<p>Curators set their own prices, which must be at least <?= e($v['min_price']) ?>. A curator may sell only what they control and can deliver. For Spotify and Apple Music playlists, a curator may sell only a listen and honest consideration of a song, never a guaranteed placement, a number of streams or a chart position. Listings are reviewed by us but we do not verify every claim and do not guarantee any curator's results.</p>
<h2>4. Bookings and payment</h2>
<p>A creative pays the curator's price plus a service fee of <?= e($v['buyer_fee']) ?> through Paystack into escrow. From the curator's price we deduct a commission of <?= e($v['curator_fee']) ?>. Fees are shown before you pay. All amounts are in Nigerian naira. See the Escrow and Refund Policy for how money is held, released and returned.</p>
<h2>5. Payouts</h2>
<p>Curators may withdraw their wallet balance, from <?= e($v['min_wd']) ?>, to a Nigerian bank account in their own name. We may delay or refuse a payout where we reasonably suspect fraud, a chargeback, a legal request or a breach of these terms, and we may be required to verify your identity.</p>
<h2>6. Disputes</h2>
<p>Either party may open a dispute while an order is in progress or delivered. While a dispute is open the money stays in escrow. We review what both sides provide and decide how the booking price is split between the curator and the creative. Our decision is final on the Platform; it does not remove your legal rights.</p>
<h2>7. No guarantees</h2>
<p>Music promotion results depend on listeners, platforms and chance. We do not guarantee streams, followers, sales, playlist adds, chart positions or any other outcome.</p>
<h2>8. Content you give us</h2>
<p>You keep ownership of your content. You give us a licence to host and display it to run the Platform. You promise you have the right to share it and that it does not infringe anyone's rights.</p>
<h2>9. Liability</h2>
<p>To the extent the law allows, our total liability to you for any claim is limited to the fees we earned from the booking the claim relates to. We are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, or for the acts of curators and creatives. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law, including your rights under Nigerian consumer protection law.</p>
<h2>10. Changes, ending, law</h2>
<p>We may update these terms and will tell you about material changes. You may close your account at any time once no orders or balance are outstanding. These terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria, and the courts of Akwa Ibom State have jurisdiction, subject to any mandatory rights you have elsewhere.</p>
